{"parentUuid":"fa8441bc-89dc-4fa8-b468-b483a19e747d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"be2a55ac-7180-4afe-8e1f-07c1f28bd2fe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FYZ827h6KR1vswD7Th2va4","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\tSupport headless auth token storage\nstate:\tDRAFT\nauthor:\tpeyton-alt\nlabels:\t\nassignees:\t\nreviewers:\tCopilot (AI) (Commented)\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t\nnumber:\t1127\nurl:\thttps://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/1127\nadditions:\t969\ndeletions:\t37\nauto-merge:\tdisabled\n--\n<!-- entire-trail-link-start -->\nhttps://entire.io/gh/entireio/cli/trails/307\n<!-- entire-trail-link-end -->\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds explicit non-keyring CLI auth paths for headless, container, and CI environments.\n\n- Adds ENTIRE_AUTH_TOKEN as the highest-priority read-only CLI API token source.\n- Adds ENTIRE_SECRETS_PATH as an opt-in file-backed token store for persistent headless login.\n- Keeps OS keyring as the default backend and does not automatically fall back to plaintext storage.\n- Makes auth status, logout, and auth revoke source-aware so env tokens are not deleted accidentally.\n- Documents the user-facing auth variables in the README.\n\nFixes #1036.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe CLI only supported OS keyring persistence for API auth. In CI and headless containers, authenticated commands could not use an environment-provided API token, and entire login could complete browser/device approval but fail when saving the token to a locked or unavailable Secret Service/keyring.\n\n## Validation\n\n- mise run check\n- mise run lint\n\n## Notes\n\nENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_TOKEN remains separate and only applies to checkpoint Git fetch and push operations.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches authentication token sourcing and logout/revoke flows; mistakes could break CLI auth or unintentionally leave stale credentials, though changes are scoped and well-tested.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Adds headless-